          "basis": "Mary's 27/07 register benchmark for the scope no supplier had quoted - 7 doors on BSW glazed-door medians (GBP 8,021) plus the 16.23 m2 CW01+D03+CW02 run on the house GBP 850/m2 curtain-walling template (GBP 13,795) - against the supplier returns that landed 28/07: Bellview 0000000513 GBP 20,861.92 net of 15% (CW run + D01 + D04 + D05-D08) plus BSW QT253508 GBP 2,381.70 (D02 patio). Identical scope both sides.",
          "lesson": "The benchmark was labelled 'a floor and not a price' and it was one, by 6.1% - the first entry where the stated direction held. But the margin is flattered: the benchmark was called low because it carried no panic hardware, pivot/concealed-closer set or master-key suiting, and the actual return turned out to carry almost none of that either (4 of 6 required BS EN 1125 devices absent, no suiting at all). So -6.1% is the gap between two prices that BOTH omit the hardware, not the gap to a compliant one. When you flag a benchmark as a floor because of missing content, check the supplier return actually contains that content before treating the comparison as closed.",
          "error_pct": -6.14,
