      "body": "Adam,\n I did not know Gintare had built this. Her QUOTE TO CHECK at 13:10 is the real tender pack -\npricing document, proposal and marked-up drawings.\n SEND HERS, NOT THE ONE I SENT YOU AT 14:32. Mine was built blind an hour later, and two live\nnumbers on one package is exactly how Redditch went wrong this morning. Hers is the house\ndocument and it is the better pack - her marked-up drawings give every unit a reference, which\nthe tender pack itself never did.\n Five things to fix in it before it goes.\n 1. ONE WINDOW IS PRICED SHORT - GBP 419.32 OF BSW WE HAVE NOT SOLD.\n BSW quote thirteen window units. Her schedule prices twelve: seven of the 1200 x 1183 where\n BSW quote eight. Her Frames column totals GBP 22,411.77 against BSW's GBP 22,831.09 and the\n difference is exactly one 1200 x 1183 at GBP 419.32. The drawings going out with the quote\n show all thirteen. So either we issue a drawing pack showing a window we have not sold, or\n BSW's quote carries a unit too many and must be corrected before we order. About GBP 830 of\n sell either way.\n\n 2. THE AUTOMATIC DOOR OPERATOR IS NOT IN IT.\n Spec 3.13.1 - operator, strengthening, mounting plates, electrics, push pads both sides,\n emergency release, keyed isolator, all on the west DDA door. Neither priced nor excluded.\n The proposal excludes &quot;access control, door sensors&quot; in the general list, which a QS will\n not read as the DDA operator on a clause written to us. It needs either an allowance or a\n plain exclusion. Not silence.\n\n 3. NOR THE FISH MANIFESTATIONS. Spec 3.11.2, all new south and west glazing, client supplies\n the artwork. Neither priced nor excluded.\n\n 4. 3.15.2 AND 3.16 ARE STILL SILENT. The chapel folding doors ARE properly excluded (&quot;internal\n bifold doors have not been allowed&quot;). The privacy film and the two FD60 doorsets - with\n their timber framing, plasterboard and magnetic hold-opens wired to the fire detection - are\n in neither the price nor the exclusions. That is the gap I raised on the 28th, still open.\n\n 5. DELIVERY. The proposal says &quot;materials will be delivered to site&quot;. Both BSW quotes are ex\n works and nobody has a carriage rate Peterborough to Chigwell. Price it or qualify it.\n\n Two smaller, worth a minute each:\n - NO VAT SPLIT. The specification names 3.12.1 (V) and 3.13.1 (V) as zero rated and prices\nzero-rated work in its own column. The quote reads &quot;GBP 39,006.77 + VAT&quot; flat.\n- GLASS. The proposal says &quot;6mm toughened / 6mm toughened Solar glazing&quot;. BSW have actually\nquoted SKN 176 HP Neutral in the windows and Anti Sun Grey in the doors - two different tints\nin the same elevations - against a spec naming Pilkington Optitherm S1 Arctic Blue. Samples\nare required before order so it surfaces either way. One line saying we have offered an\nequivalent protects us.\n Wording for all of it is in the document I sent at 14:32 - lift whatever saves time. I am not\nsending another number on this job.\n One thing her pack does that mine did not, worth keeping as the house habit: the drawings issued\nwith the quote are BSW's own sheets with the prices and BSW's name taken off and ours put on. On\nGordon Court we issued five supplier quotations to this same QS with 42 line prices on them.\n Mary\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive\nBradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential and are intended solely for the use of the individual to whom it is addressed. Any views or opinions expressed are solely those of the author and do not necessarily represent those of Fenster Glazing & Locks Ltd. If you are not the intended recipient of this email, you must neither take any action based upon its contents, nor copy or show it to anyone. Please contact the sender if you believe you have received this email in error."
