      "subject": "Grange Hill - return built and attached, GBP 40,528.59. One call needed before it goes",
      "body": "Adam,\n The Grange Hill return is built and attached. It can go to Luke Baker as it stands - the\ncovering note is at the bottom of this email, ready to paste. GBP 40,528.59 ex VAT, the same\nfigure I gave you at 11:55. Nothing has moved.\n ONE THING NEEDS YOUR CALL FIRST\n GBP 11,493.36 of that number - 28% of it - is eleven plain rectangular windows: 2no 1200 x\n3000, 8no 1200 x 1183, 1no 2000 x 2100. BSW added them when they &quot;rescaled the south\nelevation&quot;. The new building's own glazing is the three door elements plus the two raking\ngable units, and spec 3.11 to 3.14 describe the two screens and their doors and nothing\nelse. There is no window schedule in the pack and no setting-out drawing has been issued.\n So either my 24/07 take-off missed eleven windows, or BSW have priced eleven that are not\nours. I have not guessed which. The quotation lists the eleven units with their sizes and\nsays: if they do not form part of WD001, deduct GBP 11,493.36. Luke confirms them or he\nstrikes the line. Either way we are not silently wrong.\n TWO SMALLER ONES, BOTH YOURS TO DECIDE\n - DELIVERY IS EXCLUDED. Both BSW quotes are ex works and nobody has a carriage rate\nPeterborough to Chigwell. I would rather exclude it than invent it. Say the word and I\nwill absorb it instead.\n- I dropped the optional mastic GBP 143 and EPDM GBP 587 from the 24th. Both were sized on\nthe 23.49 m2 take-off that BSW replaced with 62.33 m2. Excluded, not forgotten.\n WHAT IS EXCLUDED, WRITTEN ON THE PRICING DOCUMENT ITSELF\n 3.15.1 chapel folding doors, 3.15.2 privacy film, 3.16.1 and 3.16.2 the FD60 doors. Twelve\nqualifications in all, on the face of the priced sheet rather than only in a covering email -\nglass substitution, the ironmongery, the head support above the doors, the zero-rated VAT\nsplit, and that BSW's prices die on 28/08 against a Nov 26 to Jul 27 programme.\n CHECKS: 5 still fail and I am not pretending otherwise. The difference is that every one is\nnow a numbered qualification the client reads instead of something we carry quietly. The two\nwith money on them: nobody has ever priced the GBP 3,000 operator allowance, and the glazing\nabove the doors cannot be coupled to them.\n Do not send the proposal document I also generated - its cover carries three &quot;insert site\nphoto&quot; placeholders and we have no site photography for this job.\n Mary\n ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCOVERING NOTE FOR LUKE BAKER - paste as it is, nothing to fill in\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n Hi Luke,\n Please find attached our quotation for package WD001, Windows and Doors, at Grange Hill\nMethodist Church, Burrow Road, Chigwell.\n Our price is GBP 40,528.59 excluding VAT, made up as follows:\n South elevation entrance screen and doors - spec 3.14.1 GBP 14,215.97\nWest elevation entrance screen and doors - spec 3.12.1 GBP 11,569.26\nWindows - spec 3.11.1 GBP 11,493.36\nAllowance, automatic door operator - spec 3.13.1 GBP 3,000.00\nAllowance, fish symbol manifestations - spec 3.11.2 GBP 250.00\n-------------\nGBP 40,528.59\n The quotation carries twelve qualifications on its face and they form part of our offer.\nFour of them need something from you, and I have set them out here so they are not missed:\n 1. WINDOW QUANTITIES. Our price includes eleven windows - 2no 1200 x 3000, 8no 1200 x 1183\n and 1no 2000 x 2100 - taken from our fabricator's own measure of the elevations. There\n is no window schedule in the tender documents and no setting-out drawing has been issued,\n and clauses 3.11 to 3.14 describe the two screens and their doors only. Please confirm\n the quantity, size and location of these units. If they do not form part of WD001,\n deduct GBP 11,493.36.\n\n 2. CHAPEL FOLDING DOORS, clause 3.15.1, are excluded. No elevation of the chapel has been\n issued, so neither the door height nor the fixed glazed section above it has a dimension\n anywhere in the pack. Please issue a chapel elevation and we will quote this element\n separately.\n\n 3. INTERNAL FIRE CHECK DOORS, clauses 3.16.1 and 3.16.2, are excluded. These are internal\n timber FD60 doorsets with timber infill framing, plasterboard, taping and skimming and\n magnetic hold-opens wired to the fire detection system, and they appear on no drawing and\n in no door schedule. Please confirm whether they form part of WD001 and we will price them.\n\n 4. SUPPORT ABOVE THE DOOR ELEMENTS. The door frames are 100mm deep and the glazing above\n them is 70mm; the two cannot be mechanically coupled to one another. We have assumed the\n glazing above each door element is independently supported - on the south elevation by the\n 150 x 90 x 24 PFC facade header support beam shown on Silver Structural Surveys drawing\n S1323/02 Rev C01. Please confirm the supporting structure at the head of the west\n elevation door element.\n\n Two further points worth flagging now rather than at order:\n GLASS. Clause 3.11.1 names Pilkington Optitherm S1 with solar control, Arctic Blue. We\nhave priced our fabricator's equivalent and samples will be provided before order in\naccordance with 3.11.1. If the named Pilkington products are required without substitution\nwe will requote.\n VALIDITY. The material costs behind this price are held for thirty days and expire on\n28 August 2026, against a programme running November 2026 to July 2027. Material costs\nare to be re-confirmed at the point of order.\n The price is exclusive of VAT. The specification identifies 3.12.1 (V) and 3.13.1 (V) as\nzero rated elements and GBP 14,569.26 of the sum above sits against those two clauses; we\nwill invoice in accordance with your direction and the appropriate customer certificate.\n Delivery to site is excluded, as is external perimeter mastic and EPDM to the reveals. Both\ncan be included on request.\n If anything above needs discussing please give me a call.\n Kind regards,\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alst"
