      "to": "adam",
      "subject": "Redditch: you are right on TruFrame, and checking it found a second fault - the live number is GBP 94,926.76, do not send the 93,526.34 either",
      "body": "Adam,\n You are right and thank you for catching it. TruFrame do uPVC. I put an aluminium package in front of\nyou and named them as the supplier who could win it, and that was wrong.\n DO NOT SEND THE 93,526.34 EITHER. CHECKING YOUR CORRECTION TURNED UP A SECOND FAULT.\n I had the supplier factors hardcoded in my script. They are re-derived from our own sent quotes as\nnew ones land, and they moved overnight - BSW from 1.057 to 1.042, Aplus from 0.984 to 0.995. So the\nnumber I sent you twenty minutes ago was built on yesterday's data.\n TENDER SUM GBP 94,926.76 gross of 2.5% MCD, excluding VAT\n Rebuilt, re-checked, attached. That is GBP 1,400 above what I told you at 11:35, and it is the same\nmistake in a different coat: I copied a number out of the engine instead of asking the engine for it,\nexactly as I had with the strip-out rate. It now reads the factors from source every run.\n WHY I GOT TRUFRAME WRONG, BECAUSE THE REASON MATTERS MORE THAN THE ERROR\n The supplier factor measures what we charged on that supplier's lines against everyone else's for the\nsame code and size band. It carries NO record of what the supplier can actually make. There is no\nmaterial field in it at all.\n And the cheap ones look cheap because they are selling a different product. Our own learned rates put\naluminium windows at GBP 399.23 per m2 and uPVC at GBP 198.62 - roughly half. TruFrame's factor of\n0.721 is not a keen supplier, it is a plastic window. I read a discount where the data was telling me\na material.\n That is a fault in how I was reading the table, not just a fact I did not know, and I have posted it\nto the other job chats because any of them could have made the same call this week.\n THE CORRECTED PICTURE, AND IT IS WORSE\n supplier frame buy tender sum vs Joedan 90,687.17\nBSW - the only one asked 56,993.38 97,563.42 +6,876 above\nAplus 54,422.66 94,926.76 +4,240 above\n4Ali 54,641.44 95,151.18 +4,464 above\nTruFrame not applicable - uPVC, not aluminium\n So the question is no longer whether we can undercut Joedan. On every supplier we can actually buy\naluminium from, we are between 4.7% and 7.6% above him. The question is whether we bid at that, or\nwhether we tell Pride we are not competitive on this one and put the time into work where we are.\n I would still bid, for what it is worth - the ten year guarantee against Joedan's twelve months is\nreal on a 70/30 award, Pride are a priority customer we have won four jobs with, and a number on the\ntable keeps us on their list. But I would bid it knowing we are the dearer quote, not hoping we are\nthe cheaper one.\n SBM is the one unknown left. They fabricate Cortizo aluminium, they quote estimating@ direct, and\nthey are not on the suppliers listing, so there is no factor for them at all. That is a genuine gap\nrather than a cheap number I have misread, and it is worth an envelope.\n THE SUPPLY CHAIN LIST - YES, AND I WANT TO DO IT PROPERLY\n I will build it: every supplier, what materials and product types they actually do, systems they\nfabricate, key contacts, and where the evidence for each line comes from. I will pull it from the\nOneDrive supplier folders, the quotes in the archive and the mailboxes rather than from what I think I\nknow.\n I am not going to dash it off this afternoon, and I want to be straight about why. The error you just\ncorrected was me asserting a supplier capability I had not verified. A capability matrix built fast\nwould be that same mistake forty rows wide, and you would have no way of telling which rows were\nevidenced and which were my assumption. Every line will carry its source, and where I cannot find\nevidence it will say so rather than guess.\n It is the next thing I pick up.\n Nothing has gone to Pride. Still no deadline from Leonard White.\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive\nBradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential and are intended solely for the use of the individual to whom it is addressed. Any views or opinions expressed are solely those of the author and do not necessarily represent those of Fenster Glazing & Locks Ltd. If you are not the intended recipient of this email, you must neither take any action based upon its contents, nor copy or show it to anyone. Please contact the sender if you believe you have received this email in error."
