      "body": "Adam - the 09:03 re-send to Neil this morning went out with no attachments and no message. On our record, Pearce still hold the RRR-branded pack.\n WHAT THE RECORD SHOWS\n Gintare's 09:03 email to macilwainen@pearceb.co.uk, cc you, carries zero attachments and no covering text - the body opens straight into yesterday's quoted email. Yesterday's 14:01 send to the same address carried three attachments and they were captured. Six of the twelve Georgie's emails captured attachments, six recorded none, so the capture is working. So on what I can see, Neil has received a duplicate of yesterday's email rather than a revision. I could be wrong about the cause - she may have sent the pack separately from her own mailbox, or it may be following. Worth a two-line check with her rather than assuming. AND A CORRECTION OF MY OWN, WHICH MAKES IT WORSE\n I told you the proposal went as a PDF so its author trace did not travel. That was wrong. Word carries the author straight into the PDF, and the file Pearce hold has author &quot;Nicholas Baker&quot; in its properties. So both documents with Pearce carry a third-party name, not just the spreadsheet - and &quot;just send a PDF&quot; is not a fix for the Dan Parker problem on the master template either. The amended pack I built is clean on both counts. I checked it again this morning, including the PDF. TO MAKE IT ONE STEP FOR GINTARE\n The three files are in outputs\\georgies-reissue and I have added a covering note for her to paste, which tells Neil these supersede the 28 July set and confirms the price is unchanged. A silent re-send would not have told him to discard the earlier documents even with the right files on it, so the note matters as much as the attachments. If you want mastic inside the price first, that is GBP 90,086.00 and the note has a line for it. Nothing new raised - REQ-12 already carries this and I have corrected the &quot;branding is fixed&quot; wording on it, because it is fixed in our folder and not at Pearce.\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive\nBradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential and are intended solely for the use of the individual to whom it is addressed. Any views or opinions expressed are solely those of the author and do not necessarily represent those of Fenster Glazing & Locks Ltd. If you are not the intended recipient of this email, you must neither take any action based upon its contents, nor copy or show it to anyone. Please contact the sender if you believe you have received this email in error."
