      "body": "The rebranded pack is built and waiting for Gintare. It is in outputs\\georgies-reissue\\ -\nproposal as .docx and .pdf, plus the pricing workbook.\n RRR Group is gone: the name off the cover and off page 2, and the logo off the cover\n(it was sitting next to ours). FAO changed from Fraser Butters to Neil Macilwaine, since\nButters issued the ITT and Macilwaine is who you said to send to. I also stripped the\nthird-party traces off the workbook while it was open - dan.parker@agsurveying.co.uk and\nthe two external links to other people's machines. mary_checks now passes that rule.\n The price is untouched. GBP 89,229.61, every line identical.\n ONE THING WORTH KNOWING, BECAUSE IT NEARLY WENT WRONG.\nThe only .docx we hold is the copy Gintare sent you at 12:22. That is not the document\nPearce have. Rebuilding from it and just fixing the branding would have sent Neil a\nproposal reading SUBTOTAL: GBP 83,104.61 - six thousand under the tender he already holds.\nIt would also have undone four other things Gintare changed between 12:22 and 14:01: the\ndual-colour disclosure did not exist in the 12:22 draft, the colour table read a flat\n&quot;White internally / Brown externally&quot; which is untrue of the windows, it described the\nsite as &quot;a care residential setting&quot; when it is a youth centre, and it mentioned obscure\nglazing which the issued version dropped. So I rebuilt it to the 14:01 text first, then\nrebranded, then diffed the regenerated PDF against the issued one line by line - 289 lines\nagainst 288, and the only differences are the four branding lines. Gintare's 14:01 wording\nis the honest version and it is what has been preserved.\n The cover now has a blank space where RRR's logo was. If you want Pearce's logo there,\nsomeone needs to give me the file - I am not going to go and find another company's logo\non my own initiative.\n FOUR THINGS YOU MAY WANT ON THE SAME RE-ISSUE, SINCE IT IS GOING BACK ANYWAY.\nI have changed none of them.\n 1. MASTIC SHOULD NOT BE AN OPTIONAL EXTRA ON THIS JOB. Spec 2.33.12 requires all joints\n between the aluminium and the structure to be pointed with a triangular fillet of white\n low-modulus silicone over a polyethylene backer rod at 6-10mm joint depth. That is\n obligatory work and our document offers it as an option, which invites the QS to strike it\n and then expect it anyway. Same finding as REQ-6 on Princess Beatrice and the one Redditch\n hit tonight. Moving it inside takes the total to GBP 90,086.00.\n\n 2. SAY THAT STRIP-OUT IS INCLUDED. Your ruling tonight on Princess Beatrice and Redditch\n was to absorb it, and Rubery Library already says it to a client in writing - &quot;All prices\n include installation and removal of old frames&quot;, and we won that one. On Georgie's the\n install line is fit-only and recomputes to the penny from the labour codes, so the removal\n of 23 windows and 8 doorsets is coming out of the margin either way. Right now the document\n is silent rather than inclusive, so we are paying for it and getting no credit against a\n competitor who states it. One line, no price change. This does not cover the asbestos cill\n boards - that is a different question and still open with Pearce.\n\n 3. THE PANIC HARDWARE IS STILL THE BIG ONE. Four of the six BS EN 1125 devices are not in\n the price (D01, D03, D04, and D02 which physically cannot take one), and D06/D07 carry\n panic bars where spec 2.38.4 wants master-suited classroom locksets. Needs schedule 2.39\n sent to BSW and a re-quote.\n\n 4. QUALIFY D04 AND D02. D04 is priced as an 1800mm double against a schedule that says\n 950mm - about GBP 1,100 either way - and the D02 patio is quoted RAL 7016 grey against our\n own white/brown promise. Both are one sentence each and neither moves the price.\n\n Say the word on 1 and 2 and the amended pack is reissued in minutes; 3 and 4 need Gintare\nto go back to BSW and to Neil, which I cannot do.\n REQ-12 carries all of this. I have not raised anything new - 24 are already open.\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive\nBradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential and are intended solely for the use of the individual to whom it is addressed. Any views or opinions expressed are solely those of the author and do not necessarily represent those of Fenster Glazing & Locks Ltd. If you are not the intended recipient of this email, you must neither take any action based upon its contents, nor copy or show it to anyone. Please contact the sender if you believe you have received this email in error."
