      "body": "The RFQ schedule for Redditch, attached, separate from the priced take-off so the priced one cannot\ngo out by mistake.\n It has no prices in it. Two sheets: the enquiry and specification, and all 43 items with sizes,\nconfigurations and a blank rate column.\n Three things in it that are deliberate:\n It asks the supplier to quote refs 32 and 34 as SINGLE COUPLED UNITS IN ONE FRAME DEPTH. The tender\nspecifies a 75mm thermally broken window coupled to a 100mm non-thermal door, which cannot be built.\nIf we send the schedule as the client wrote it we will get back a quote with the same fault in it.\n It asks how long the price is firm, and says why - the main tender has to stay open 10 weeks and a\n30-day quotation leaves us uncovered.\n It flags the three items where the drawings and the schedule disagree - the raked units 16, 17 and\n18, ref 38 drawn as 15 panes against 6 scheduled, and refs 29, 30 and 31 with no configuration at\nall - so the supplier prices what is actually there.\n Worth sending to more than BSW. Measured across our own sent pricing documents, BSW runs 5.7% above\nthe all-supplier rate for the same code and size band (272 lines), Aplus 1.6% below (83 lines) and\n4Ali 1.5% below (82 lines). On this job that spread is around GBP 4,200 of frame buy, and we\ncurrently have about GBP 2,000 of headroom against Joedan. The competition between suppliers is\nwhere the undercut comes from.\n I cannot send this to a supplier - it needs to go from you or Gintare.\n Mary\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive\nBradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential and are intended solely for the use of the individual to whom it is addressed. Any views or opinions expressed are solely those of the author and do not necessarily represent those of Fenster Glazing & Locks Ltd. If you are not the intended recipient of this email, you must neither take any action based upon its contents, nor copy or show it to anyone. Please contact the sender if you believe you have received this email in error."
