      "body": "Checked. Before anything else: the quote you asked me to check is not the quote Pearce have.\n You were sent it at 11:22. It went to Neil Macilwaine at 13:01, cc you. The version on your\ndesk totals GBP 83,104.61. The version Pearce hold totals GBP 89,229.61. The GBP 6,125.00\ndifference is three deliberate uplifts added after your copy left: +GBP 75.00 on each of the\n23 windows (GBP 1,725), +GBP 2,000 on the curtain walling run, and a new GBP 2,400 line for\nKingspan cavity closers. Reconciles to the penny. Nothing is wrong with adding margin - but\nthe closers have no supplier quote behind them, and the uplifts were typed over the template\nformulas, so the issued workbook no longer recomputes.\n Good news first, because there is some. BSW came back at 09:45 and the 35.45 m2 that had no\nprice yesterday now does: Bellview 0000000513 at GBP 20,861.92 net of 15% for the CW run and\nsix doors, plus BSW QT253508 at GBP 2,381.70 for the D02 patio. With Mercury that is\nGBP 50,562.65 of supply behind a GBP 89,229.61 tender. All 31 units are covered - 23 windows,\n8 doorsets, the screen run. Nothing is missing on count. The workbook that went out is\nvalues-only, so no supplier cost or margin column leaked to Pearce. And Gintare disclosed the\nsingle-colour sash problem to Pearce in the covering email rather than burying it, which was\nthe right call.\n Now the six things that need you.\n 1. FOUR OF THE SIX PANIC BARS ARE NOT IN THE PRICE, AND TWO DOORS HAVE ONE THEY MUST NOT HAVE.\n Spec 2.39 schedules internal push-bar panic exit devices to BS EN 1125 on D01, D02, D03, D04,\n D05 and D08, and thumbturn with classroom function - 5-lever mortice, external cylinder, 316\n stainless escutcheon, suited to the building's existing master key - on D06 and D07.\n Bellview put a concealed panic bar on the four 950mm singles, which their quote lines up as\n D05, D06, D07, D08. So D05 and D08 are right. D06 and D07 have a panic bar where the spec\n wants a master-suited lockset. And D01, D04, D03 (the door in the screen run) and D02 have no\n panic device at all - handles, hold-open closers and cylinders keyed alike, nothing more.\n D02 is the awkward one: it is a 2-rail sliding patio with an inline patio lock and it cannot\n physically take a BS EN 1125 push-bar. That one is a question for the CA, not a price.\n BSW told us this would happen, in writing: &quot;there is also no hardware schedule, so I have\n assumed single doors to be fire escapes based on the floor plans.&quot; The hardware schedule\n exists. It is spec 2.39 and nobody sent it to them. The concealed bar needs a different door\n leaf build (IMP041 stile plus the anti-finger-trap push-bar profile), so this is not a part\n we bolt on later - it is a rebuild of four leaves. No master-key suiting is bought anywhere;\n &quot;keyed alike&quot; means keyed alike to each other, not to the building's suite.\n\n 2. STRIP-OUT IS NOT FUNDED AND ASBESTOS IS NEITHER PRICED NOR EXCLUDED.\n The install line is GBP 8,614.73 and it recomputes exactly from the house labour codes with\n zero residual - CW 16.2315 m2 x GBP 150 = GBP 2,434.73, 23 windows x GBP 160, D02 and the two\n doubles at GBP 500, the four singles at GBP 250. Same control as Princess Beatrice. That\n money is fit-only, so on a job where 23 windows and 8 doorsets have to come out first, the\n removal is unpriced - and the exclusions schedule does not exclude it either. Worse, spec\n 2.43.1 says the internal cill boards throughout the building are asbestos containing and the\n contractor &quot;shall allow to include within the tender submission for the removals&quot;. That is an\n express, non-provisional requirement sitting inside our scope. Our exclusions do not mention\n asbestos at all. Pearce carry a separate Asbestos Removal element and a GBP 5,000 defined\n provisional sum, so it may well be theirs - but nothing on our document says so, and our\n installers cannot lift those windows without disturbing the boards.\n\n 3. THE U-VALUE IS THE POINT OF THIS JOB AND WE HAVE NOT CLAIMED IT.\n PSDS4 decarbonisation scheme. Spec 2.28, 2.33.5 and 2.38.3 all require a maximum area-weighted\n 1.6 W/m2K and say we must provide evidence of the energy efficiency rating. The proposal\n recites the requirement and never confirms we meet it. Mercury still state no U-value at all\n and quote &quot;Clear Lam Tgh&quot; with no low-E or soft coat named. Bellview and BSW state Ug 1.0 and\n 1.1 - that is centre-pane glass, not the whole-element Uw the spec asks for. So we have no\n element U-value from any of the three, and a reglaze would be ours.\n\n 4. THE DOCUMENT PEARCE HOLD SAYS THEY ARE SOMEBODY ELSE.\n The proposal title page reads &quot;Prepared For RRR GROUP&quot; and page 2 reads &quot;Client: RRR Group&quot;.\n It went to Pearce Construction. Separately, the pricing workbook carries\n dan.parker@agsurveying.co.uk as its author and two external links to\n C:\\Users\\LiamO'Donnell\\... and C:\\Users\\Parke\\... - visible in file properties without opening\n it. That is REQ-27, and this is the third job this week to go out carrying it, because the\n template was never fixed. The proposal went as a PDF so its own author trace did not travel;\n the .xlsx did.\n\n 5. THE PATIO DOOR IS QUOTED GREY.\n BSW QT253508 gives D02 as Ext Colour RAL 7016 Grey with no internal colour stated. Our own\n proposal colour table promises &quot;Doors/CW - White internally / Brown externally&quot;. True of the\n Bellview items (inside WP, outside Brown), not true of the door we actually bought. The\n colour disclosure Gintare made to Pearce covers only the sash windows.\n\n 6. D04 IS PRICED AS A DOUBLE AT 1800mm AGAINST A SCHEDULE THAT SAYS 950mm.\n Gintare read the &quot;Double Doorset&quot; description over the scheduled width, and BSW priced two\n 1800 doubles to match. That is the expensive reading - GBP 4,109.76 against GBP 3,021.31 - and\n it is not qualified anywhere on the issued document. If the schedule is right we are carrying\n about GBP 1,100 of air; if the description is right, a"
