      "body": "Dear Harry\n Hill - Supply Base Key Documents have expired \n Please update expired certificates and documents to ensure you remain an active member of the Hill supply base. The information that we currently hold is shown below:\n SSIP Expiry - 01 Sep 2024 BS OHSAS 18001 Expiry -\n Employers Liability Insurance - 19 Aug 2026 Public Liability Insurance - 19 Aug 2026 Professional Indemnity Insurance -\n Product Liability Insurance -\n All Risks Insurance -\n Other Insurance -\n If you have updated your details on Constructionline in the last 7 days, please ignore this e-mail.\n Instructions for Suppliers with a Constructionline profile Please log in to your Constructionline profile https://conl.portals.assessment-services.co.uk/#/authenticate. Once logged in to Constructionline you will be able to see on the Summary page which sections require updates under the various sections, such as; insurance details, health and safety, financial information, etc. Please review each section carefully completing the information and uploading supporting documentation as required. Please make sure you have submitted the section before logging out of the system. Once submitted and verified by Constructionline the information will synchronise with the Hill system and update your information. If you have any issues with the Constructionline system please call the helpdesk on 0333 300 3066 and they will be able to assist with your query. Instructions for Suppliers that do not have a Constructionline profile Help If you need to contact Hill for any reason please contact supplychain@hill.co.uk\n Thank you in advance for completing the information requested.\n Hill Supply Chain Team \n The terms of use of Tradex is available here: Terms of use \n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDisclaimer Notice :-\n\nThe message and any attachments contained in this e-mail are intended for the named recipient(s) only. It may contain privileged or confidential information or information which is exempt from disclosure under the applicable laws. If you are not the intended recipient(s), you must not read, print, retain, copy distribute, forward or take any or refrain from taking any action in reliance on it or any of its attachments. If you have received or have been forwarded this e-mail in error, please notify us immediately by return e-mail or telephone (+44 (0)1628 552000) and delete this message from the computer or any other data-reading device in its entirety.\n\nPlease advise us immediately if you do not or your employer does not consent to Internet e-mail for messages of this nature.\n\nInternet communications cannot be guaranteed to be secure and error-free as the information could be intercepted, corrupted, lost, arrive late or contain viruses. The sender and this Company therefore do not and shall not accept any liability or responsibility of whatsoever nature in the context of this message and any attachment(s) which arises as a result of Internet transmission. \n\nRegistered Office: Sterling House, 20 Station Road, Gerrards Cross, Buckinghamshire, SL9 8EL\nRegistered in England No: 3921897 www.causeway.com"
