        "what": "Chiel Construction, Swanshurst School sports hall glazing, GBP 52,483.33 ex VAT - AdminBase lead 7384, Chris Mitchell, chris@chielcon.co.uk",
        "why_not": `There is a named contact, a live quote and a real ask on the table - and I still cannot write the first line, because it swings entirely on a fact I cannot see. Jayk's repricing log (19/12/2025) says "Chris at Cheil has asked us for PQQ's to be completed and for updated costs + schedule". The PQQ paperwork ARRIVED on 18/12/2025 and a revised quote is dated 22/12/2025; nothing in commercial@, info@ or jacob@ shows any of it going back, and jayk@ is a 404. If the pack never went, the honest opening is delivering it 223 days late. If it went, this is an ordinary chase. Those are not two wordings of one email, they are two different emails, and D-1 died the same morning for being written on a premise nobody had checked. I am not making that mistake twice in one session.`,
        "next": "JAC-19 - Adam or Mary confirms whether the completed PQQ pack, the revised costs and the schedule left estimating@ after 18/12/2025. Asked of Mary on the bot line 30/07. The moment it is answered this becomes a draft, and it carries a second item either way: Birmingham 2026/02027/PA, a new SEN teaching facility at the same school, undecided with consultation closing 05/08/2026. Nothing goes to Chiel before the answer. data/companies/chiel-construction.md."
